{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:3d0a871d7233f3542a63cf13171c2f5b597dbf567ea75f6d9740c0cd7657f15e","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026#in:resolution","title":"Finite conditional resolution"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/0b23de156108ea5bf3ce9ad8.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:eb85d3603ec7254e8723f8292d2014fbb295087c537d4a9a7c22689061a82822","id":"r:Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026:in:resolution","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026","name":"Finite conditional resolution","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.2","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/introduction.tex","label":"in:resolution","line":94,"manuscript":"Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026","statement_sha256":"c45a7e282294a18fc969d504e8ec08a85ad65aa008ddc7afd2de5cedb20afcef"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026.html#in:resolution","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:7bc97827d9b792686e310af9a5634927badc242c9742a18b24ede529c1859aa4","file":"preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":94,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"c45a7e282294a18fc969d504e8ec08a85ad65aa008ddc7afd2de5cedb20afcef","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7bc97827d9b792686e310af9a5634927badc242c9742a18b24ede529c1859aa4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L94"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{in:resolution}\nFix the preceding band geometry and use the critical plus-boundary law\nin a larger reference square. For every $\\epsilon,\\eta>0$, one can\nchoose contour levels in any prescribed separated subwindows,\na finite descriptor $Z^\\delta\\in\\{0,1,\\ldots,m\\}$, and regular\nsigned barriers $\\Gamma_1,\\ldots,\\Gamma_m$ with the following properties\nfor all sufficiently fine meshes.\n\nThe exceptional state $0$ has probability at most $\\epsilon$. For every\ntranscript in a good state $i\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$, insert the plus pins of $\\Gamma_i$ and\nthen its minus pins. The sum of the two resulting total-variation\nchanges on the target is at most $\\eta$. The final target-side law\n$Q_{i,\\delta}$ is the same for every transcript in that state.\nConsequently this conclusion holds simultaneously for all bounded target\nobservables, including mesh-dependent observables. For any fixed finite\nlist of bands the descriptors have convergent joint laws.\n\nThe finite list of barriers and its positive geometric clearances are\nchosen before the mesh threshold. If another law has band density at\nmost $K$ times the reference density, its exceptional probability is\nat most $K\\epsilon$."}
